{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 39, :comments ["The reason for <b>ak.</b> Because in the preceding pericah he mentioned affliction of the soul, he forbade fasting on the festival of Sukkot, for in it are written 'and you shall rejoice' and 'you shall rejoice' and 'you shall be nothing but joyful.'" "<b>When you gather the produce of the land.</b> Fields and vineyards." "<b>taḥogu.</b> Doubled-stem forms, and the meaning concerns the sacrifices." "<b>On the first day, a sabbath-rest.</b> A noun, and it lacks 'it shall be for you.' Had it been an attributive noun, there would be a heh in place of the bet."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:12:01.561442065Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}